course: dictionary
lesson: 2358
title: One word, more than one meaning
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many English words have more than one meaning. The word cuckoo can name a bird, a clock, or a silly person. To find the right meaning, read the words around it. Those words are its context, and they usually give the clue.
explain: «The call of lush meadow-grass, wet orchards, warm, insect-haunted ponds ... the cuckoo's note» is set in the countryside, so the cuckoo must be a bird, and its note is the sound it calls. A cuckoo clock would not be found in a meadow.
explain: Check your meaning by putting it into the sentence. If it still makes sense, you have the right one. Also notice when a word is informal: «go cuckoo» is chatty speech meaning go crazy, so it would not appear in a formal report about birds.
fact: Some words have more than one meaning, and context tells you which one is meant.
fact: Cuckoo is a noun for a grey bird whose call sounds like «cuck-oo».
fact: Some cuckoos lay their eggs in other birds' nests, so other birds raise their chicks.
fact: A cuckoo clock has a little bird that pops out and calls the hours.
fact: Informally, «cuckoo» is an adjective meaning silly or crazy, as in «go cuckoo».
exercise: «a desert bird of the cuckoo family that would rather run than fly» Here, what does cuckoo family tell you? | A kind of nest | A group of people who are silly | *A group of birds that are related to each other | A family that owns a clock
exercise: Ben says his sister has gone cuckoo because she is shouting at a spider. What does cuckoo mean here? | A grey bird with a call | A famous tree | *Crazy or silly | A little bird that pops out of a clock
exercise: Find and copy the one word from «Others are tricksters: a cuckoo leaves its egg for a small reed warbler to raise» that means someone who fools other people. | warbler | reed | *tricksters | egg
test: In a cuckoo clock, what is the cuckoo? | A grey bird with a call | A tree in a meadow | A silly person | *A little bird that pops out and calls the hours
test: A cuckoo in the nest is someone who does not belong and takes over. What does this phrase mean? | A bird that sings in the morning | A nest made from grass | *Someone who does not belong and takes over | A kind of clock
exam: Which sentence uses cuckoo as an informal word meaning silly? | Grandad wound the cuckoo clock every Sunday. | *Dad says that plan is totally cuckoo! | The cuckoo sang at the top of the oak tree. | The cuckoo laid an egg in the warbler's nest.
